  "notes": [
    "Hollin Bay (#12, #36): the open bay, the control venue. Open water to the south and west, the shore curving round the north and east, a lighthouse on the western headland. Little shore effect and no current.",
    "Venue frame: metres, x east, y north. Directions are compass bearings in degrees. Schema: docs/venue-file.md.",
    "Classic oscillating: the gradient wind from the west-south-west, blowing onshore. Sea breeze: onshore from the south-west, veering as it fills in.",
    "Geographic grids, one per pairing (#10): the shore's light touch, the wind slowing by up to 14 % and bending by up to 2 deg close in to it. Land is downwind in both pairings, so there is no land shadow: over the race areas the wind is within 1 % and 1 deg of the open bay's.",
    "Checked offline (#83): the longest beat's race area at every seeded rotation (+-10 deg) stays clear of land and inside each grid, and the course is sailable in a 25 % lull."
